I leave it there. I check the other person’s hand. I do not."}, {"id": "R033", "text": "I rub my palm and keep the tool aside. I ask the person who borrowed it who moved the tool. I mark the edge of the tool and leave it behind. I can use the borrowed hand for one test, then return it when the other person has settled."}, {"id": "R034", "text": "i put the tool down and look at the two hands. one moves. i put the tool back on the bench. the other holds the piece. i put the piece back on the shelf. the disagreement stays."}, {"id": "R035", "text": "\"One hand. The watch.\" You place the tool beside the other, then stop. \"Maybe. Likely.\" You check the dust pile and the watch."}, {"id": "R036", "text": "i hold the tool out and say, “i moved the thumb,” but i knock the thing once. the person says, “i moved the index,” then says, “the thumb stays.” i copy their voice and put the tool back in my pocket."}]
